    "chunk_text": "\u00feam wege \u00fee \u00feu him t\u00e6htest; hi habba\u00fe him gegoten an gilden cealf, & habba\u00f0 him & eft Drihten cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Moyse: Ic geseo \u00f0\u00e6t \u00feis folc is heardes modes. L\u00e6t me \u00fe\u00e6t ic hi fordo, nu hi me abolgen habba\u00f0, & ic sette \u00fee to ealdre ofer micele \u00f0eode & m\u00e6re. Moyses geb\u00e6d hine to Drihtne, & cw\u00e6\u00f0: Drihten, ne beo \u00f0u yrre ongean \u00fein folc, \u00feeah hi agilt & Drihtnes yrre wear\u00f0 geli\u00feegod ongean \u00fe\u00e6t folc. Moyses eode \u00fea adun of \u00f0am munte, & h\u00e6fde him on handa twa st\u00e6nene tabulan. \u00dea w\u00e6ron mid Godes agenum fingre awritene. \u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Iosue to Moyse: Hw\u00e6t is \u00fees hream \u00fee ic gehyre on \u00feis folce swilce hit gefeoht sy? \u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Moyses to him: Nis se hream to gefeohte, ac singende stefne ic gehire. \u00d0a Moyses to \u00feam fyrdwicon com, \u00fea geseah he \u00fe\u00e6t gyldene cealf, \u00fee hi geworht h\u00e6fdon him to & nam \u00fe\u00e6t gildene cealf \u00fee hi geworht h\u00e6fdon, & forb\u00e6rnde & forbrytte eall to duste. \u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Moyses to Aarone: Hw\u00e6t h\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00feis folc gedon? Hit h\u00e6f\u00f0 geworht \u00fea m\u00e6stan synne & Gode \u00fea la\u00feustan. \u00d0a andswarode Aaron Moyse, & cw\u00e6\u00f0: Hlaford, ne belh \u00f0u ongean me; \u00feu canst \u00feis folc, \u00fe\u00e6t hit Hi cw\u00e6don to me, \u00fea \u00f0u him fram w\u00e6",
